      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gays Mills is nestled in the scenic Kickapoo Valley and is celebrated for its historic charm and apple orchards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gaysmills.gov/discover/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "James Gay founded the village by building a dam and a sawmill on the Kickapoo River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gays_Mills%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gays Mills was named in honor of its founder, James Gay, and his brothers, John and Thomas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gays_Mills%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Twining family of Gays Mills gained fame after showcasing their apples at the World's Fair.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gays_Mills%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Numerous commercial apple orchards surround Gays Mills, making the area a significant center for apple growing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gays_Mills%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Thomas Gay and his family organized the First Congregational Church, the first church established in Gays Mills.",
